# Letter 1 content
body_1 = """
  <p class="body-p">
    It is my distinct pleasure to write this letter of academic recommendation in strongest support of <strong>Mr. Fuad Ahmed</strong> for admission to the Master of Science degree program in Computer Science and Technology under the Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC Type B) or University Fellowship.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    I am an Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer in the Department of Computer Science at St. Mary’s University. I have known Fuad for over three years during his undergraduate studies in Computer Science, where I instructed him in advanced computing modules including <em>Advanced Database Systems, Operating Systems, and Advanced Object-Oriented Programming</em>, in addition to evaluating his senior software assessments.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Throughout his undergraduate tenure, Fuad consistently stood out as one of the most disciplined, intellectually rigorous, and inquisitive students in his cohort. He graduated with a strong <strong>Major Cumulative GPA of 3.20 / 4.00</strong>, earning top grades (<strong>A/A+</strong>) across core computational theory, system architecture, and database courses. What distinguished Fuad was not merely high examination scores, but his deep conceptual curiosity and systematic approach to software engineering.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    In practical laboratory modules, Fuad demonstrated exceptional capability in relational database internals, transaction semantics, and algorithmic optimization. While many students struggled with race conditions and concurrency bottlenecks, Fuad independently researched and implemented atomic locking mechanisms (pessimistic row-locking with transactional boundaries) to preserve absolute financial ledger integrity. His senior capstone work mirrored this high standard, earning highest departmental marks for modular design, clean separation of concerns, and robust error handling.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Beyond curriculum coursework, Fuad is an exceptionally self-driven engineer who expanded his competencies into mobile applications (Flutter/Dart) and scalable backend services. He communicates technical ideas with clarity, maturity, and intellectual humility, frequently assisting classmates during complex debugging sessions.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    I give <strong>Mr. Fuad Ahmed my highest and unreserved recommendation</strong> for admission and scholarship consideration. I am confident he will prove to be an outstanding, dedicated researcher in your graduate laboratory.
  </p>
"""

# Letter 2 content
body_2 = """
  <p class="body-p">
    I am writing this letter to recommend <strong>Mr. Fuad Ahmed</strong> with great enthusiasm for admission to your Master of Science program in Computer Science and Technology / Software Engineering, supported by the Chinese Government Scholarship (CSC) or University Fellowship.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    As an Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer in the Faculty of Informatics at St. Mary’s University, I served as Fuad’s instructor for <em>Web and Internet Programming, Software Engineering Methodology, and Distributed Applications</em>, and advised him across multiple departmental programming projects.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    During his studies at St. Mary’s University, Fuad demonstrated remarkable aptitude for software engineering principles and systems architecture. In my classes, he consistently demonstrated an ability to synthesize abstract theoretical computer science concepts into robust, well-engineered production code. His project submissions in web technologies and software design patterns were characterized by elegant modularity, adherence to Test-Driven Development (TDD) principles, and comprehensive documentation.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Fuad's academic record speaks for itself—achieving an <strong>A</strong> grade in Web &amp; Internet Programming and maintaining a strong <strong>3.20 Major GPA</strong> across his core computing subjects. What impresses me most about Fuad, however, is his dedication to continuous self-improvement and technical problem-solving. While still an undergraduate, he actively mastered cross-platform mobile frameworks (Flutter) and backend architectures (Laravel/REST), independently architecting solutions to solve real-world challenges in Addis Ababa, such as crowdsourced geospatial mapping and offline-first mobile synchronization.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Furthermore, Fuad exhibits exceptional character, integrity, and cultural adaptability. He collaborates effectively with classmates, often taking the lead in debugging complex system interactions and mentoring junior peers in version control and software best practices. His English communication skills, both written and oral, are proficient, as his entire undergraduate degree was conducted strictly in the English medium of instruction.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    China’s leading universities are at the forefront of distributed systems, cloud computing, and intelligent mobile infrastructure. Fuad possesses precisely the intellectual resilience, hands-on programming rigor, and inquisitive mindset required to thrive in a high-intensity research laboratory. I wholeheartedly recommend <strong>Mr. Fuad Ahmed</strong> for admission and scholarship consideration.
  </p>
"""

html_1 = get_html(
    dept_name="Department of Computer Science",
    ref_code="CS",
    subject="Academic Recommendation for Mr. Fuad Ahmed (Master of Science in Computer Science)",
    course_examples="Advanced Database Systems and Operating Systems",
    rank_example="Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    body_paragraphs=body_1,
    signer_title="Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    signer_dept="Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Informatics"
)

html_2 = get_html(
    dept_name="Department of Computer Science &amp; Software Engineering",
    ref_code="SE",
    subject="Letter of Recommendation for Mr. Fuad Ahmed (MSc Software Engineering / Computer Science)",
    course_examples="Web and Internet Programming, Software Engineering Methodology",
    rank_example="Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    body_paragraphs=body_2,
    signer_title="Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    signer_dept="Department of Software Engineering, Faculty of Informatics"
)

# File paths
h1_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, 'letter_1.html')
h2_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, 'letter_2.html')

with open(h1_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html_1)
with open(h2_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html_2)

print('Wrote HTML templates.')

# Convert HTML -> ODT -> DOCX & PDF
for i, h_path in enumerate([h1_path, h2_path], start=1):
    base_name = f'Fuad_Ahmed_Recommendation_Letter_{i}_StMarys'
    odt_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, f'letter_{i}.odt')

    # 1. HTML -> ODT
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'odt', h_path, '--outdir', scratch_dir], check=True)

    # 2. ODT -> DOCX (in output_dir)
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'docx', odt_path, '--outdir', output_dir], check=True)
    # Rename to friendly name
    raw_docx = os.path.join(output_dir, f'letter_{i}.docx')
    target_docx = os.path.join(output_dir, f'{base_name}.docx')
    if os.path.exists(target_docx):
        os.remove(target_docx)
    os.rename(raw_docx, target_docx)
    print(f'Generated: {target_docx}')

    # 3. ODT -> PDF (in output_dir)
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'pdf', target_docx, '--outdir', output_dir], check=True)
    print(f'Generated PDF: {base_name}.pdf')

print('All recommendation letters generated successfully!')

