    During his studies, Fuad demonstrated remarkable aptitude for software engineering principles and systems architecture. In my classes, he consistently demonstrated an ability to synthesize abstract theoretical computer science concepts into robust, well-engineered production code. His coursework in web technologies and design patterns was characterized by elegant modularity, adherence to Test-Driven Development (TDD), and comprehensive documentation.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Fuad's academic record speaks for itself—achieving an <strong>A</strong> grade in Web &amp; Internet Programming and maintaining a strong <strong>3.20 Major GPA</strong> across his core computing subjects. What impresses me most about Fuad is his dedication to continuous self-improvement. While still an undergraduate, he actively mastered cross-platform mobile frameworks (Flutter) and backend architectures (Laravel/REST), independently architecting solutions to solve real-world challenges in Addis Ababa, such as crowdsourced geospatial mapping and offline-first mobile synchronization.
  </p>

  <p class="body-p">
    Furthermore, Fuad exhibits exceptional character, integrity, and cultural adaptability. His English communication skills are proficient, as his entire undergraduate degree was conducted strictly in the English medium of instruction. I wholeheartedly recommend <strong>Mr. Fuad Ahmed</strong> for admission and scholarship consideration.
  </p>
"""

html_1 = get_html(
    dept_name="Department of Computer Science",
    ref_code="CS",
    subject="Academic Recommendation for Mr. Fuad Ahmed (Master of Science in Computer Science)",
    body_paragraphs=body_1,
    signer_title="Associate Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    signer_dept="Department of Computer Science, Faculty of Informatics"
)

html_2 = get_html(
    dept_name="Department of Computer Science &amp; Software Engineering",
    ref_code="SE",
    subject="Letter of Recommendation for Mr. Fuad Ahmed (MSc Software Engineering / Computer Science)",
    body_paragraphs=body_2,
    signer_title="Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer",
    signer_dept="Department of Software Engineering, Faculty of Informatics"
)

# File paths
h1_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, 'letter_1.html')
h2_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, 'letter_2.html')

with open(h1_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html_1)
with open(h2_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html_2)

# Convert HTML -> ODT -> DOCX & PDF
for i, h_path in enumerate([h1_path, h2_path], start=1):
    base_name = f'Fuad_Ahmed_Recommendation_Letter_{i}_StMarys'
    odt_path = os.path.join(scratch_dir, f'letter_{i}.odt')

    # 1. HTML -> ODT
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'odt', h_path, '--outdir', scratch_dir], check=True)

    # 2. ODT -> DOCX (in output_dir)
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'docx', odt_path, '--outdir', output_dir], check=True)
    raw_docx = os.path.join(output_dir, f'letter_{i}.docx')
    target_docx = os.path.join(output_dir, f'{base_name}.docx')
    if os.path.exists(target_docx):
        os.remove(target_docx)
    os.rename(raw_docx, target_docx)
    print(f'Generated: {target_docx}')

    # 3. DOCX -> PDF
    subprocess.run(['libreoffice', '--headless', '--convert-to', 'pdf', target_docx, '--outdir', output_dir], check=True)
    print(f'Generated PDF: {base_name}.pdf')

print('All recommendation letters updated and converted successfully!')

